{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact Mac installed-roots head 554a2666faae0460b12c7b2c06bf00cacb95ce13 on builder/mac-installed-roots-20261103, tree 9ec4ca15, for request 5ed8de03 under promise d558e857 and review request 78e7215e. This approval covers the optional INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES setting in prepare-github.mjs and deploy.py, their tests and docs/self-host.md. It claims no G3b packet, no staging with a real App key and no deployment.\n\nScope. Main ecf59e05 is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. Against main, the head changes the two Mac validators, their two test files, docs/self-host.md, the note and two manifests. The commit-message check passes for both commits. No card path changes. From the gate commit 25146ccf to the head, only docs/self-host.md, the note and the gate manifest change.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- prepare-github.mjs admits INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES as a second optional variable. When the variable is present, the project stage calls the production readInstalledRegisters through the pinned loader and refuses anything except \"pinned\". The check runs inside originalProject, before the App key is read. The refusal case points the key path at a file that does not exist and gets a project-stage refusal for each of six bad lists, with no output directory.\n- Staging copies the setting's exact bytes, whitespace included, and the real Python prepared_project then accepts the staged project.\n- deploy.py applies the same contract: a string of at most 4,096 UTF-8 bytes, a JSON list of 1 to 32 distinct canonical Scope IDs, and the current REGISTER_SCOPE in the list. A lone surrogate refuses through the same named error. The setting joins the required set only when present, so the exact variable allowlist still refuses an unrelated variable.\n- The two checks agree on canonical form. The Python pattern requires a final a or q, and production isScopeId refuses the same \"…b\" ID in the noncanonical case. Where the two checks could drift, deploy.py refuses, so a drift blocks a deploy instead of admitting a list.\n- Without the setting, both validators behave as before. Every original case and check stays.\n- The JavaScript control disables the production-parser call and fails at \"missing current root\". The Python control removes the uniqueness and current-root clause and fails at \"deployment refuses missing current root\". Each starts from 7 passes, records 6 passes and one assertion failure, and restores the exact file. The control baselines c62e3cd1… and 5aa076ec… equal the two validators at the head.\n\nThe gate passed. gate.exit at 25146ccf reads exit 0 after 1,815 seconds. source-before and source-after both record tree 03add0b2 and a clean status. Node 133, Counting 56, plain 3,601 with one skip and Native 1,065 with two skips all pass. Both Vitest phases report zero unhandled errors, and reconciliation reports no issue and no failed case. The gate reports no EnvironmentTeardownError. One passing gate identifies no cause for the archive-scale failure, so 64552d40 stays open.\n\nEvidence. The two manifests hash to 7f42972a… and 50223ca8…, and the note names both. All 27 public files match their sizes and digests and are read-only, both SHA256SUMS files match, and no unit holds an unlisted file. All 29 private files match their index. The focused checks ran on the uncommitted change over ecf59e05, and their recorded bytes for all four source and test files equal the head. The scan for private keys, GitHub tokens and bearer values finds no match. The tests use synthetic RSA syntax and contact no App or provider.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Staging uses the production parser, and the deploy boundary keeps its own closed allowlist. The operator's reviewed list still decides which roots keep creating children.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The list reaches no Native authority or GitHub binding. A bad list refuses before the helper touches the App key, and a project that skips staging still meets the Python check.\n\